DTSTAMP:20261116T045100Z
DTSTART:20261119T204000Z
DTEND:20261119T210000Z
SUMMARY:! Metro: Midosuji Line\, Namba → Shin-Osaka
DESCRIPTION:ARRIVE 06:00: Shin-Osaka\, Nozomi 308 departs 06
 :39\nLEAVE 05:40. Midosuji Line\, Namba → Shin-Osaka (¥280 e
 ach)\n\nTICKET (Klook): Nozomi 308\, 06:39\, booked for 6. O
 pen the Klook booking. If it says QR boarding: each person s
 cans their own QR at a Shinkansen gate with the QR mark and 
 keeps it for the exit at Tokyo. If it says pick-up: scan the
  QR at a JR ticket machine first to print 6 paper tickets (a
 llow 10-15 min). iPhone: turn off Express Transit before sca
 nning. Midosuji Line: tap your own Suica/ICOCA. Buy breakfas
 t at PLUSTA inside the gate.\n\nROUTE: Osaka Metro Midosuji 
 Line (M\, red) from Namba M20\, platform for 梅田・新大阪 (Umeda /
  Shin-Osaka)\, 7 stops to Shin-Osaka M13. Leave the hotel by
  05:40\, which leaves about 40 min at the station before the
  06:39: this is a booked train\, so keep that room. Buy brea
 kfast (ekiben) and drinks at Shin-Osaka before the 06:39 (sh
 op hours at 06:00 not checked) or at Tokyo Station after 09:
 06.\n\nSTEP BY STEP:\n- Walk: APA Hotel → Namba Station (Mid
 osuji Line\, M20) (2 min · ≈150 m). The hotel page says 2 mi
 nutes. Metres are minutes x 75.\n- Wait: Wait at Namba M20 p
 latform (~3 min) [estimate]. Early-morning Midosuji trains r
 un every few minutes.\n- Ride: Osaka Metro Midosuji Line (M\
 , red): Namba M20 → Shin-Osaka M13\, 7 stops (via Shinsaibas
 hi\, Hommachi\, Yodoyabashi\, Umeda\, Nakatsu\, Nishi-Nakaji
 ma-Minamigata) (15 min · ¥280). Take the platform for 梅田・新大阪
  (Umeda / Shin-Osaka).\n- Walk: Shin-Osaka M13 → JR Shin-Osa
 ka Shinkansen gates (follow 新幹線) (5 min · ≈350 m) [estimate]
 . Inside the station\; the metro exit and the Shinkansen gat
 es are connected.\n\nTODAY'S FIXED POINTS:\n- Nozomi 308\, 0
 6:39 (booked). At Shin-Osaka by 06:00: about 40 min to spare
 . Leave the hotel by 05:40.\n- Fujikyu bus\, 09:50 (booked).
  The Nozomi arrives 09:06: 44 min to spare for the walk to t
 he Yaesu South terminal (about 10–15 min\, est.) and the que
 ue. A train delay of up to about 25 min is absorbed.\n- Chur
 eito sunset\, 16:33. Plan: the 14:25 Fujikyu train\, deck ab
 out 15:10\, 83 min before sunset. If the Red Line back from 
 Oishi is late or full\, the 14:58 Fuji Kaiyu (limited-expres
 s ticket) reaches the deck about 15:45 and the 15:16 local a
 bout 16:00\; the 15:56 is after sunset. So two later trains 
 still work.\nIF RUNNING LATE:\n- Bus into Kawaguchiko late: 
 take the Red Line at 12:30 instead of 12:15 (Oishi Park shri
 nks from 60 to 45 min).\n- Not at Kawaguchiko by about 13:00
 : skip Oishi Park\, eat houtou or take-away by the station a
 nd take the 14:25 (or the 14:58 / 15:16).\n- Lunch at Oishi 
 running long: take the 13:57 Red Line and the 14:58 or 15:16
  train\; eat the rest on the way.\n- After the pagoda nothin
 g is fixed. Honcho Street at dusk (20 min) goes first.\n- Di
 nner has 128 min of room (17:45–19:53): take the 20:23\, 20:
 52 or 21:34 Fujikyu train instead of 19:53\; the last is 23:
 51. Check-in at Fuga A is contactless.\n\nFull plan\, maps a
 nd live changes: https://japan-trip-app-wine.vercel.app/
LOCATION:Shin-Osaka Station
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:! Metro: Midosuji Line\, Namba → Shin-Osaka
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
