 a baggage counter\nLEAVE 09:24. Skyliner about 09:20\, Keise
 i-Ueno → Airport Terminal 2·3\, about 10:01 (¥2310 each)\n\n
 TICKET: Skyliner e-ticket (to buy): swap the voucher for sea
 t tickets at the Keisei-Ueno counter or Code Exchange machin
 e by about 09:00. On a full train\, seats together are not g
 uaranteed.\n\nROUTE: Skyliner from Keisei-Ueno (KS01) at abo
 ut 09:20\, all seats reserved: book the exact train for Sun 
 22 Nov (Keisei renumbers the Skyliners on 21 Nov). Get off a
 t 空港第2ビル Airport Terminal 2·3 (KS41)\, about 41 min later. G
 o up to the departures floor and leave the suitcases at a ba
 ggage storage counter (手荷物一時預かり)\, about ¥1\,000 a suitcase 
 for the day (est.\; not checked).\n\nSTEP BY STEP:\n- Walk: 
 Grids (with suitcases) → Keisei-Ueno Station (Ameyoko market
  on the way) (9 min · ≈600 m). The hotel page says about 9 m
 in. Metres are minutes x 70 with suitcases.\n- Wait: Wait at
  Keisei-Ueno (~21 min) [estimate]. Swap the Skyliner voucher
  at the counter or the Code Exchange machine from 09:00 (abo
 ut 15 min)\, then wait for the train at about 09:20.\n- Ride
 : Keisei Skyliner (all seats reserved): Keisei-Ueno KS01 ~09
 :20 → Airport Terminal 2·3 KS41 ~10:01 (41 min · ¥2\,310). T
 rain number not checked after the 21 Nov timetable change.\n
 - Walk: Terminal 2·3 station (B1) → Baggage counter\, T2 (4 
 min · ≈300 m) [estimate]. Queue about 15 min (est.).\n\nFull
  plan\, maps and live changes: https://japan-trip-app-wine.v
 ercel.app/
